Spec: Node Edit Tool

Purpose:
  Direct manipulation of individual anchor points and control handles on paths.

Owns:
  ./node.ts
  ./node.test.ts

Must:
  Click selects a single node.
  Shift+click adds/removes from node selection.
  Drag moves selected nodes.
  Arrow keys nudge selected nodes by 1px (Shift+Arrow for 10px).
  C key sets node type to Corner.
  S key sets node type to Smooth (colinear handles, independent lengths).
  Y key sets node type to Symmetric (colinear handles, equal lengths).
  Delete removes selected nodes from path.
  Double-click on segment inserts a new node.
  Click on a segment (away from its endpoint nodes) selects the segment,
    independent of node selection.
  Hovering a node or segment highlights it (ring on node, colored stroke on
    segment) before it is clicked.
  Dragging a selected segment translates it rigidly (both endpoint nodes and
    their control handles move together), rather than reshaping it into a curve.
  All node edits are undoable.

Must not:
  Allow editing nodes of grouped shapes without entering the group.
  Move nodes of locked shapes (future).
  Create new shapes.

Depends on:
  @BaseTool
  @IEditorContext
  @MoveNodeCommand
  @DeleteNodeCommand
  @ChangeNodeTypeCommand
  @InsertNodeCommand

Scenario: click to select node
  Given a rectangle path is selected and NodeEdit tool is active
  When the user clicks on the top-left node
  Then that node is highlighted as selected

Scenario: drag to move node
  Given a node is selected in NodeEdit mode
  When the user drags the node by (+20px, +20px)
  Then the node's position updates by that delta
  And connected segments update accordingly

Scenario: arrow nudge
  Given a node is selected
  When the user presses the Right arrow key
  Then the node moves 1px to the right
  When the user presses Shift+Right
  Then the node moves 10px to the right

Scenario: change node type to smooth
  Given a corner node is selected
  When the user presses 'S'
  Then the node type changes to 'smooth'
  And the control handles become colinear

Scenario: change node type to corner
  Given a smooth node is selected
  When the user presses 'C'
  Then the node type changes to 'corner'
  And the control handles become independent

Scenario: delete node
  Given a rectangle with 4 nodes and one node selected
  When the user presses Delete
  Then the path has 3 nodes
  And the shape remains valid

Scenario: insert node on segment
  Given a path with a straight segment between nodes A and B
  When the user double-clicks the midpoint of that segment
  Then a new node is inserted between A and B
  And the path now has one additional node

Scenario: move node with undo
  Given a node is selected at position (100, 100)
  When the user drags it to (150, 150) and presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the node returns to (100, 100)

Scenario: multi-select with shift
  Given two nodes visible on a path
  When the user clicks node A, then Shift+clicks node B
  Then both nodes A and B are selected
  And dragging moves both simultaneously

Scenario: break path at node
  Given a closed rectangle with 4 nodes and one node selected
  When the user triggers "Break Path" at that node
  Then the path becomes open at that point

Scenario: click segment to select it
  Given a rectangle path is selected and NodeEdit tool is active
  When the user clicks the middle of the top edge (away from its endpoints)
  Then that segment is selected
  And no nodes are selected

Scenario: hover highlights node or segment
  Given NodeEdit tool is active on a selected path
  When the mouse moves over a node without clicking
  Then that node is rendered with a hover ring
  When the mouse moves over a segment without clicking
  Then that segment is rendered highlighted

Scenario: drag segment translates it
  Given a segment is selected in NodeEdit mode
  When the user drags the segment by (+0px, +20px)
  Then both endpoint nodes and their control handles move by that delta
  And the segment does not bow into a curve

Tasks:
  [x] Click to select node.
  [x] Multi-select with Shift.
  [x] Drag to move nodes.
  [x] Arrow nudge (nudges selected nodes, not the whole shape).
  [x] Node type switching (C/S/Y).
  [x] Delete node.
  [x] Insert node on segment.
  [x] Segment to Line / Curve conversion.
  [x] Break path at node.
  [x] Click segment (independent of nodes) to select it.
  [x] Hover highlight for nodes and segments.
  [x] Segment drag translates rigidly instead of curving.
